            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0338" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1124.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-31T23:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Lower House of Congress filibustering against passage of legislation attempt to
                    control apportionment of representation in electoral college, no election being
                    possible until such apportionment. The filibustering is intended to prevent
                    election before April 30th. Parties opposed to Government proposing to claim
                    office of President vacant after 30th, however. Government reports serious
                    fighting begun at La Vega and Santiago.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
